{"type":"message","id":"54f1b05b","parentId":"71098868","timestamp":"2026-04-14T08:04:30.154Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to set up the configuration so that image understanding uses MiniMax-V06. Let me check the current config and figure out how to set it up properly.\n\nCurrently the config has:\n- `agents.defaults.model.primary` = \"minimax/MiniMax-M2.7\"\n- `agents.defaults.imageModel.primary` = \"minimax/MiniMax-V06\"\n\nSo actually the image model is already configured to use MiniMax-V06! The user might just be confirming they want this setup, or they might not know it's already set up this way.\n\nWait, but I need to check if this is actually how it works. \n\nLooking at the models list, MiniMax-M2.7 only supports text input, while MiniMax-V06 supports both text and image. And the imageModel.primary is already set to MiniMax-V06. So the config looks correct already - images should automatically route to V06 and text to M2.7.\n\nBut the user is asking to set this up, which makes me wonder if they're experiencing issues with image recognition not working properly. Let me verify the actual config to see if it matches what I'm seeing.","thinkingSignature":"fe6b73623ab811f047a600468d31d427c68f938efdb13c22a71ea8a63c893f54"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_v7u9ixg6uaca_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nimport json\nwith open('/Users/edy/.openclaw/openclaw.json') as f:\n    data = json.load(f)\n    agents = data.get('agents', {}).get('defaults', {})\n    print('primary model:', agents.get('model', {}).get('primary'))\n    print('image model:', agents.get('imageModel', {}).get('primary'))\n\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":92,"output":343,"cacheRead":42905,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":43340,"cost":{"input":0.0000276,"output":0.0004116,"cacheRead":0.0025743,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0030134999999999997}},"stopReason":"t