{"type":"message","id":"45ecef36","parentId":"12b4c11c","timestamp":"2026-04-14T08:09:31.575Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So the configuration shows that:\n1. V06 has `input: ['text', 'image']` which means it's configured to support images\n2. But the error says \"Unknown model: minimax/MiniMax-V06\"\n\nThis suggests there's a mismatch - the model is defined in the config, but when the image tool tries to use it, it gets \"Unknown model\". \n\nThe log also showed `model not allowed: minimax/MiniMax-V06` at one point (09:14:03), and then at 14:56:31 there was a config reload.\n\nWait - the \"Unknown model\" error might be coming from the image tool itself, not from the OpenClaw system. \n\nI think the issue is that when I called the `image` tool, OpenClaw tried to route it to minimax/MiniMax-V06 but the model wasn't actually registered or available in the system. Let me check if there's a model allowlist or blocklist that's preventing this.","thinkingSignature":"72a4d1a19746c9901659c19fa0031a2df7e5b46788f7d4576326b45a14313178"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_qnoetsrlzg17_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nimport json\nwith open('/Users/edy/.openclaw/openclaw.json') as f:\n    data = json.load(f)\n    # Check if there's any model restriction/allowlist\n    print('Full agents.defaults:')\n    print(json.dumps(data.get('agents', {}).get('defaults', {}), indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))\n\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":21733,"output":307,"cacheRead":26151,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":48191,"cost":{"input":0.0065198999999999995,"output":0.0003684,"cacheRead":0.00156906,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.008457359999999999}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1776154160022,"responseId":"062d2931607535dc1ed100d1cb5044d2"}}
