{"type":"message","id":"8f50d862","parentId":"0681662f","timestamp":"2026-04-14T08:42:20.171Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The Minimax API key is not stored in the workspace credentials directory. It must be stored elsewhere by OpenClaw - perhaps in the gateway's own credential store. Since the system prompt says the model is working (I can respond to text), the API key must be accessible to the gateway.\n\nLet me try to test the image URL approach directly. Since I can't easily get the API key, let me think about what I can test:\n\n1. I could try uploading the image to a public URL and then using that\n2. I could check if there's a way to call the image tool with a URL instead of a local file\n\nActually, the user's point is very valid - the issue might be with the Feishu media download + routing. Let me try using the `image` tool with a URL instead of a local file path to see what happens.\n\nBut first, I need the actual Minimax API key. Let me check if OpenClaw stores it somewhere accessible.","thinkingSignature":"ef5f65b92f6f2254a67afd5d52b1211cea654fe877eea98b92c98d3eb495f112"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_n5e6x1zhhejb_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Check OpenClaw's internal credential storage\nfind ~/.openclaw -name \"*.key\" -o -name \"*.pem\" -o -name \"credentials.json\" 2>/dev/null | grep -v backup | head -5\n# Also check if gateway stores its own credentials\nls ~/.openclaw/*.json 2>/dev/null"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":25365,"output":295,"cacheRead":26151,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":51811,"cost":{"input":0.0076095,"output":0.000354,"cacheRead":0.00156906,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00953256}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1776156126383,"responseId":"062d30e04724e852ebf1d22bf75d1838"}}
