{"type":"message","id":"13e62d82","parentId":"5c01fa57","timestamp":"2026-04-14T08:42:50.480Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I can't easily get the Minimax API key. But based on the user's analysis, let me think about what the real issue might be.\n\nThe user has a good point - \"Model does not support images\" could be coming from M2.7 (the primary model), not V06. When OpenClaw routes the image, it might first check if the primary model (M2.7) supports images, and if not, it tries to route to imageModel (V06). But if the API call itself fails for V06 (maybe the API key doesn't have V06 permissions), then it would report \"Model does not support images\" for V06.\n\nBut actually, looking at the error again:\n```\n[media-understanding] image: failed (0/1) reason=Model does not support images\n```\n\nThe \"(0/1)\" likely means 0 out of 1 providers succeeded for media understanding. So it's saying none of the configured providers for media understanding support images.\n\nAnd then:\n```\n[tools] image failed: Unknown model: minimax/MiniMax-V06\n```\n\nThis suggests V06 wasn't found at all when the image tool tried to use it.\n\nGiven the user says:\n1. M2.7 has image understanding via understand_image MCP\n2. OpenClaw says it auto-connects to MiniMax image MCP\n3. There are community issues about this exact problem\n\nThe most likely issue is that OpenClaw's image tool is trying to use V06 as a vision model, but the API key doesn't actually have V06 permissions - OR - the OpenClaw version (2026.4.2) has a bug where it checks model capabilities incorrectly.\n\nSince the user wants me to help diagnose further, let me test with a URL if possible. Let me try to see if there's a way to access the image via URL in the current session.","thinkingSignature":"ed6b407a88c65dd70196be24de7752d1cd9f0e96b2678f832045829e57497580"},{"type":"text","text":"\n频哥，我想到一个测试思路——**不用本地文件，直接用 URL 方式调用 image 工具**。如果 V06 本身可用，URL 方式应该能工作：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_e8m9xxclyh1m_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Generate a temporary public URL for the test image\n# Check if openclaw has a built-in media hosting\ncat ~/.openclaw/openclaw.json | python3 -c \"\nimport sys, json\nd = json.load(sys.stdin)\nprint('Media config:', json.dumps(d.get('media', {}), indent=2))\nprint('Plugins:', list(d.get('plugins', {}).get('entries', {}).keys()))\n\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":25933,"output":533,"cacheRead":26151,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":52617,"cost":{"input":0.007779899999999999,"output":0.0006395999999999999,"cacheRead":0.00156906,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00998856}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1776156149074,"responseId":"062d30f6333dcaa3e7418b8afce6628c"}}
