{"type":"message","id":"ed418e28","parentId":"d6083145","timestamp":"2026-04-14T08:43:45.973Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me check the dist folder for the actual Minimax provider code. The error says \"Unknown model: minimax/MiniMax-V06\", which suggests that when the image tool tries to use the model, it can't find it in the available model list from the API endpoint.\n\nActually, thinking about this more carefully - the OpenClaw system knows about V06 (it's in the config), but when it actually tries to call the API, the Minimax API returns that V06 is \"unknown\". This could mean:\n\n1. The API key doesn't have V06 permissions\n2. V06 is a separate endpoint/model that needs to be explicitly enabled\n3. The API key is for a specific set of models and V06 isn't in that set\n\nThe user is saying that MiniMax's documentation says the Plus subscription should have image understanding via the understand_image MCP. But if V06 specifically isn't available with this API key, then maybe:\n\n- M2.7 with understand_image MCP = one approach\n- V06 as a separate vision model = another approach\n- The API key might only support M2.7 and not V06\n\nLet me check the OpenClaw Minimax provider to understand how it handles image models.","thinkingSignature":"3f85c766373e028702c96d53721089e6b98d28f045be109642aefe5861ff808e"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_tzz65veaw648_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -r \"MiniMax-V06\\|V06\\|image.*model\\|vision\" /usr/local/lib/node_modules/openclaw/dist/ 2>/dev/null | grep -v \".map\" | head -20"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":27370,"output":318,"cacheRead":26151,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":53839,"cost":{"input":0.008211,"output":0.0003816,"cacheRead":0.00156906,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.01016166}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1776156211758,"responseId":"062d31357db04726483b0c3810090e44"}}
