{"type":"message","id":"e969ab27","parentId":"40ec559b","timestamp":"2026-04-14T08:54:44.420Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to research how to fix the image understanding issue on my own. Let me think about what I know and what I can research.\n\nThe issue is:\n1. When sending an image via Feishu, OpenClaw tries to use MiniMax-V06 for image understanding\n2. But the error says \"Unknown model: minimax/MiniMax-V06\" \n3. The MiniMax API key doesn't seem to have V06 available\n\nKey insight from the user: \n- M2.7 is described as a \"text model\"\n- Image understanding is via `understand_image` MCP tool\n- OpenClaw's image tool \"automatically connects to MiniMax's image understanding MCP\"\n   \nSo the real problem might be that OpenClaw is trying to call V06 as a chat model when it's actually just an image understanding MCP tool, and the API key might not even have V06 available. Let me dig into the OpenClaw documentation and check if there's a specific way the image tool should be configured for MiniMax.\n\nLooking at that line from the compiled code, OpenClaw does seem to recognize that V06 supports image input since it checks `model.input?.includes(\"image\")`. But the \"Unknown model\" error is puzzling—it could mean the model exists in the config but the actual API key doesn't have permission to use it, or there's something else blocking access.\n\nI'm noticing there are two different error messages happening at different stages: the media-understanding layer fails first with \"Model does not support images,\" then the image tool itself fails with \"Unknown model.\" This suggests the issue might be with how the API key is configured or what permissions it actually has, rather than a problem with the model definition in the config.\n\nThe user's mention of `understand_image` being an MCP tool rather than a native model is significant. It suggests that MiniMax's image understanding might work differently than a standard model call, which could explain why the API key isn't being recognized properly even though it should have access.\n\nI'm also noticing that OpenClaw has a `minimax` plugin in the config, and I'm wondering if that's where the V06 support is actually handled. Rather than digging through the codebase without access, I should focus on practical solutions: either finding a way to configure the image tool to use an MCP client instead of trying to call V06 as a native model, or exploring alternative image understanding providers that might integrate more smoothly with OpenClaw.\n\nWait, I'm seeing something in the error logs that might be the key here. There are mentions of MCP and image understanding in the package files, and one of the plugins listed is actually called `minimax`. This could be a separate plugin specifically for Minimax's capabilities, and it might need to be installed separately or configured differently than I initially thought.\n\nLooking at the models provider configuration, V06 is defined there with image support, but maybe Minimax's image understanding doesn't work through the standard model API at all. It might be that Minimax exposes image understanding as its own dedicated endpoint or MCP tool, separate from the chat completions endpoint, which would explain why the standard model probe is failing even though the capability exists.\n\nLet me check if there's documentation for how Minimax's image understanding API is supposed to be called.","thinkingSignature":"b2e59b5cc448da91c926ebd91bfd4a3a39afd0bf6a70879c875985d773fc7adb"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_av25strunws1_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"find /usr/local/lib/node_modules/openclaw -name \"*.js\" -newer /usr/local/lib/node_modules/openclaw/package.json 2>/dev/null | xargs grep -l \"minimax\\|MiniMax\" 2>/dev/null | head -5"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":92,"output":746,"cacheRead":63463,"cac