{"type":"message","id":"ff70ad12","parentId":"10df9fad","timestamp":"2026-04-14T08:55:57.745Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is very revealing! The default model for image understanding is `MiniMax-VL-01`, NOT `MiniMax-V06`! \n\nThe media understanding provider uses `MiniMax-VL-01` (a Vision Language model) by default, while OpenClaw's configuration has `MiniMax-V06` set as the image model. \n\nSo the issue is:\n1. OpenClaw's openclaw.json has `MiniMax-V06` configured as the image model\n2. But the Minimax media-understanding-provider actually uses `MiniMax-VL-01` as the default model\n3. When the image tool is called, OpenClaw tries to use V06, but the Minimax API doesn't recognize V06 for image understanding (V06 might only be for chat, not vision)\n\n\n4. Even though the providers config declares V06 supports image input, the actual Minimax API endpoint doesn't accept it for vision tasks—it expects VL-01 instead\n\nThe error message about V06 being unknown suggests the API itself is rejecting the model identifier, likely because Minimax's image understanding endpoint has specific model requirements that don't include V06.\n\nSo the real problem is that OpenClaw's image tool is trying to send image requests through the chat completions API with V06 as the model, but Minimax's vision endpoint doesn't recognize V06—it only works with VL-01. The media-understanding-provider should be routing to a different endpoint entirely, but something in the configuration or the tool's implementation is bypassing that and going straight to the chat API instead. The issue is that OpenClaw is trying to call V06 through the chat completions endpoint for image tasks, but Minimax's API doesn't recognize V06 in that context—it only accepts specific vision models like VL-01 there. The real problem seems to be in how OpenClaw routes image requests: it checks if the model supports image input, then calls the completions API, but for Minimax's vision capabilities, the endpoint or model name might need to be different from just passing \"MiniMax-V06\" directly. Looking at the model definitions file to see what model IDs are actually configured for Minimax's image capabilities.","thinkingSignature":"9f301d120fcd700a8717c2add636fe43023f9fba644d1a21e8ed34c37acbd9c7"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_2lcgqd678zoi_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cat /usr/local/lib/node_modules/openclaw/dist/extensions/minimax/model-definitions.js | head -50"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":39388,"output":494,"cacheRead":26151,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":66033,"cost":{"input":0.0118164,"output":0.0005928,"cacheRead":0.00156906,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.01397826}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1776156937508,"responseId":"062d340b92e48fe8d6f9b62a5eb935d6"}}
