{"type":"message","id":"5e0bdcd2","parentId":"4b88964b","timestamp":"2026-04-14T08:56:51.850Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I can see exactly what's happening! Let me trace the flow:\n\n1. When image is sent via Feishu, `describeImageWithModel` is called\n2. It first tries `resolveImageRuntime(params)` which:\n   - Finds the model from the registry (looks up `minimax/MiniMax-V06`)\n   - Checks if model supports image input\n   - If model not found → throws `Unknown model: minimax/MiniMax-V06`\n   - If model doesn't support images → throws `Model does not support images`\n\n3. If the error is `Unknown model` AND the model is a Minimax VLM model (`isMinimaxVlmModel`), it falls back to `resolveMinimaxVlmFallbackRuntime` and then calls `describeImagesWithMinimax`\n   \nLooking at the error logs, I'm getting `Model does not support images` initially, then `Unknown model: minimax/MiniMax-V06`. The sequence suggests `resolveImageRuntime` found the model but it doesn't support images, then the fallback check for Minimax VLM also fails. Let me examine what `isMinimaxVlmModel` actually validates to understand why the fallback isn't triggering.","thinkingSignature":"1774b9a9af575ac04fe9501aeb13751e42e563d803a54d16d2819625ad925bc1"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_03iqvyadv7zx_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -n \"isMinimaxVlmModel\\|MiniMax-VL\\|MiniMax-V06\\|VL-01\" /usr/local/lib/node_modules/openclaw/dist/minimax-vlm-DVRSM8ID.js 2>/dev/null | head -30"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":42255,"output":324,"cacheRead":26151,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":68730,"cost":{"input":0.0126765,"output":0.00038879999999999996,"cacheRead":0.00156906,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.01463436}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1776156986802,"responseId":"062d3442641d50f075097bad4c255bf6"}}
