{"type":"message","id":"9e117acd","parentId":"3e2b0b48","timestamp":"2026-04-14T08:57:04.813Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Found it! The `isMinimaxVlmModel` function checks if:\n1. The provider is a Minimax VLM provider (isMiniMaxVlmProvider)\n2. AND the modelId is EXACTLY `\"MiniMax-VL-01\"`\n\nSo the logic is:\n- If model is `MiniMax-VL-01` → use `minimaxUnderstandImage` (the special MCP-based image understanding)\n- If model is anything else (like V06) → use the regular `complete()` function (chat completions API)\n\nBut V06 is configured as `minimax/MiniMax-V06` which is NOT `MiniMax-VL-01`, so it's NOT recognized as a Minimax VLM model. Therefore it falls through to the regular `complete()` path, which calls the chat completions API with V06.\n\nThe problem: **V06 doesn't support image input in the chat completions API** (it's only a text model). So when the `complete()` function tries to send an image with V06, it fails because V06 can't accept images in the standard chat completions endpoint.\n\nThe fix options:\n1. Change the image model from `MiniMax-V06` to `MiniMax-VL-01` in openclaw.json\n\n\n2. Or configure something else that works\n\nI need to check if `MiniMax-VL-01` is actually available in the Minimax API and what the `minimaxUnderstandImage` function actually does.","thinkingSignature":"7a9bd05636769e271deb86b60e694326771d21a7e98f90e3488c9a9a0b48a041"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_rzoyj6k41oo9_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -n \"minimaxUnderstandImage\\|MiniMax-VL-01\\|understand_image\" /usr/local/lib/node_modules/openclaw/dist/minimax-vlm-DVRSM8ID.js 2>/dev/null | head -30"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":42729,"output":375,"cacheRead":26151,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":69255,"cost":{"input":0.012818699999999999,"output":0.00045,"cacheRead":0.00156906,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.01483776}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp